<!-- Static DOM retained for existing feature runtime. Keep IDs and classes stable. -->
<template>
<section v-pre id="tprmView" class="view">
          <div class="page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">CYBERSECURITY GOVERNANCE</p><h2>Third-Party Risk Management (TPRM)</h2><p class="lede">Kelola risiko keamanan siber dari vendor, supplier, partner, dan pihak ketiga dalam satu ruang kerja.</p></div><span class="file-count">TPRM</span></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">RISK SCORING SYSTEM</p><h3>Weighted TPRM risk summary</h3><p class="muted">Total risk score = (Vendor Tier x 35%) + (CIA Risk Score x 40%) + (Related Risk Score x 25%).</p></div></div><div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><table class="tprm-tier-table"><tbody><tr><td>35%</td><td><strong>Component A: Vendor Tier</strong><small>Tier 1 (High) = 100, Tier 2 (Medium) = 50, Tier 3 (Low) = 10.</small></td></tr><tr><td>40%</td><td><strong>Component B: CIA Risk Score</strong><small>Uses the CIA score on a 0-100 scale. Lower CIA maturity scores produce higher risk contribution.</small></td></tr><tr><td>25%</td><td><strong>Component C: Related Risk</strong><small>Very Low = 1, Low = 2, Medium = 3, High = 4, Very High = 5.</small></td></tr></tbody></table></article><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">RELATED RISK SUB-SCORE</p><h3>Risk rating calculation</h3></div></div><p class="muted">Sub-score = ((Very Low x 1) + (Low x 2) + (Medium x 3) + (High x 4) + (Very High x 5)) / (jumlah related risk x 5) x 100.</p><p class="muted">The summary is shown in color before the Actions column in the Third-party risk workspace.</p></article></div>
          <div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">PURPOSE & SCOPE</p><h3>Trusted partner governance</h3></div></div><p class="muted">Framework ini mengatur vendor yang mengakses, memproses, atau mengembangkan sistem dengan data PII dan OT, termasuk software developer partners, SaaS, cloud, logistics, dan payroll providers.</p><div class="tprm-tags"><span>GDPR Article 28</span><span>CCPA Service Provider</span><span>PII & OT data</span><span>Audit readiness</span></div></article><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">POLICY OWNER</p><h3>CISO + Procurement + Legal</h3></div></div><p class="muted">Version 1.0 · Internal — Confidential</p><p class="muted">Review cadence: annual, dan setiap terjadi perubahan material pada vendor atau data flow.</p></article></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">VENDOR LIFECYCLE</p><h3>Four-phase control model</h3></div></div><div class="tprm-lifecycle"><article><b>01</b><h4>Selection & Due Diligence</h4><p>Questionnaire, technical review, risk scoring, dan keputusan GO / NO-GO.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h4>Contracting</h4><p>DPA, audit rights, breach SLA, sub-processor approval, dan insurance.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h4>Ongoing Monitoring</h4><p>Quarterly reviews, annual audits, scorecard, KPI, dan escalation.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h4>Offboarding</h4><p>Data return/deletion, access revocation, certificate, dan post-termination audit.</p></article></div>
          <div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">DUE DILIGENCE CRITERIA</p><h3>Trusted software developer partner</h3></div></div><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Certifications</strong><span>ISO 27001, SOC 2 Type II, atau equivalent</span></li><li><strong>Security program</strong><span>Security Officer/DPO, incident response, breach SLA <= 48 hours</span></li><li><strong>Manufacturing domain</strong><span>OT/IoT security, IEC 62443, industrial protocols</span></li><li><strong>Secure development</strong><span>SAST, DAST, dependency scanning, OWASP Top 10</span></li><li><strong>Financial stability</strong><span>Cyber Liability Insurance >= $5M</span></li></ul></article><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">RISK TIERING</p><h3>Risk scoring model</h3></div></div><table class="tprm-tier-table"><tbody><tr><td>0-40</td><td><strong>High Risk · Tier 1</strong><small>Enhanced due diligence, annual on-site audit, quarterly review, CISO approval</small></td></tr><tr><td>41-70</td><td><strong>Medium Risk · Tier 2</strong><small>Standard due diligence, annual remote audit, biannual review</small></td></tr><tr><td>71-100</td><td><strong>Low Risk · Tier 3</strong><small>Simplified due diligence, annual questionnaire, triennial audit</small></td></tr></tbody></table></article></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">SCOPE</p><h3>In scope and out of scope</h3></div></div><div class="excel-wrap"><table class="excel-table tprm-framework-table"><thead><tr><th>In scope</th><th>Out of scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Software developers: custom ERP/MES, IoT platforms, analytics, cloud</td><td>Commodity suppliers, unless they process PII</td></tr><tr><td>SaaS providers hosting or processing PII</td><td>Office supplies and non-IT services</td></tr><tr><td>Cloud infrastructure providers such as AWS and Azure</td><td>Janitorial/facilities, unless they access secure areas</td></tr><tr><td>Logistics partners receiving customer or shipping data</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Payroll and HR processing vendors</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Any vendor with logical or physical access to PII</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">DUE DILIGENCE PROCESS</p><h3>Questionnaire to GO / NO-GO</h3></div></div><div class="tprm-lifecycle"><article><b>01</b><h4>Vendor questionnaire</h4><p>Self-attestation covering data processing, sub-processors, certifications, incidents, SDLC, and continuity.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h4>Technical review</h4><p>Validate evidence, penetration tests, vulnerability management, access controls, and architecture.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h4>Risk scoring</h4><p>Score PII exposure, security maturity, financial stability, and reputation from 0 to 100.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h4>GO / NO-GO</h4><p>Approve, reject, or require remediation and CISO approval before onboarding.</p></article></div><div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><table class="tprm-tier-table"><tbody><tr><td>40%</td><td><strong>PII/Data Exposure</strong><small>Volume, sensitivity, access level, and data subject count</small></td></tr><tr><td>30%</td><td><strong>Security Maturity</strong><small>Certifications, pen tests, vulnerability program, incident history</small></td></tr><tr><td>10%</td><td><strong>Financial Stability</strong><small>Revenue, years in business, and insurance coverage</small></td></tr><tr><td>20%</td><td><strong>Reputation & References</strong><small>Client references, public breaches, and legal actions</small></td></tr></tbody></table></article><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">QUESTIONNAIRE</p><h3>Minimum coverage</h3></div></div><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Data processing</strong><span>Scope and sub-processor inventory</span></li><li><strong>Security evidence</strong><span>Certifications, audit history, and incidents</span></li><li><strong>Secure SDLC</strong><span>Required for software developers</span></li><li><strong>Continuity</strong><span>Business continuity and disaster recovery</span></li></ul></article></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">CONTRACTING</p><h3>Required contractual provisions</h3></div></div><div class="excel-wrap"><table class="excel-table tprm-framework-table"><thead><tr><th>Clause</th><th>Requirement / purpose</th><th>Reference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Data Processing Agreement (DPA)</td><td>Mandatory for all PII processors</td><td>Standard DPA Template</td></tr><tr><td>Processing Instructions</td><td>Only on documented instructions from Company</td><td>GDPR Art. 28(3)(a)</td></tr><tr><td>CCPA Service Provider</td><td>No sale/sharing; limited use; no data combination</td><td>CCPA Section 1798.140</td></tr><tr><td>Audit Rights</td><td>Annual and for-cause audit at Company discretion</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Sub-Processor Approval</td><td>Prior written consent and same DPA obligations</td><td>GDPR Art. 28(2)</td></tr><tr><td>Breach Notification</td><td>Within 48 hours of discovery</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Data Return/Deletion</td><td>Within 30 days; Certificate of Deletion required</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Liability & Indemnification</td><td>Vendor liable for breach fines, penalties, and remediation</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>International Transfers</td><td>SCC/DPF incorporated where applicable</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Cyber Liability minimum $5M per occurrence</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">SOFTWARE DEVELOPER CLAUSES</p><h3>Additional control requirements</h3></div></div><div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Code Ownership & IP</strong><span>Company retains custom code and derivative works</span></li><li><strong>Backdoor Prohibition</strong><span>No undisclosed access, telemetry, or data exfiltration</span></li><li><strong>Secure SDLC</strong><span>OWASP SAMM or equivalent with security gates</span></li></ul></article><article class="insight-panel"><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Code Escrow</strong><span>Source code escrow for critical systems</span></li><li><strong>Developer Access</strong><span>Least privilege, session logs, background checks</span></li><li><strong>Change Management</strong><span>PIA for changes affecting PII processing</span></li></ul></article></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">ONGOING MONITORING</p><h3>Cadence, KPI, and escalation</h3></div></div><div class="excel-wrap"><table class="excel-table tprm-framework-table"><thead><tr><th>Activity</th><th>Tier 1 High</th><th>Tier 2 Medium</th><th>Tier 3 Low</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Security questionnaire</td><td>Quarterly</td><td>Biannual</td><td>Annual</td></tr><tr><td>Evidence request</td><td>Annual</td><td>Annual</td><td>Biannual</td></tr><tr><td>On-site/Remote audit</td><td>Annual on-site</td><td>Annual remote</td><td>Triennial</td></tr><tr><td>Performance review</td><td>Quarterly</td><td>Biannual</td><td>Annual</td></tr><tr><td>Security scorecard</td><td>Continuous</td><td>Continuous</td><td>Not required</td></tr><tr><td>Dark web / breach monitoring</td><td>Continuous</td><td>Continuous</td><td>Not required</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATORS</p><h3>Required targets</h3></div></div><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Availability</strong><span>>= 99.9%</span></li><li><strong>P1 response</strong><span>< 4 hours</span></li><li><strong>P1 resolution</strong><span>< 24 hours</span></li><li><strong>Unauthorized PII access</strong><span>0 events</span></li><li><strong>Critical vulnerability</strong><span>< 48 hours</span></li><li><strong>DSAR support</strong><span>< 5 business days</span></li></ul></article><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">MONITORING TOOLS</p><h3>Continuous monitoring</h3></div></div><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Security ratings</strong><span>BitSight, SecurityScorecard</span></li><li><strong>Threat intelligence</strong><span>Recorded Future, Mandiant</span></li><li><strong>Vendor risk platform</strong><span>OneTrust, ServiceNow GRC, ProcessUnity</span></li></ul></article></div>
          <div class="excel-wrap"><table class="excel-table tprm-framework-table"><thead><tr><th>Escalation trigger</th><th>Escalation path</th><th>Response</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Incident affecting Company data</td><td>CISO -> Privacy Officer -> CEO</td><td>Immediate, within 2 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Critical vulnerability unpatched &gt; 7 days</td><td>CISO -> Vendor escalation</td><td>24 hours</td></tr><tr><td>DPA non-renewal or expiration</td><td>Procurement -> Legal -> CISO</td><td>48 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Financial distress or bankruptcy</td><td>Procurement -> CISO -> CEO</td><td>3 business days</td></tr><tr><td>Unapproved sub-processor</td><td>Privacy Officer -> Legal</td><td>24 hours</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">OFFBOARDING</p><h3>Triggers and checklist</h3></div></div><div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Triggers</strong><span>Termination, non-renewal, bankruptcy, material DPA breach, or in-sourcing</span></li><li><strong>Required actions</strong><span>Data export, access revocation, deletion certificate, monitoring removal</span></li><li><strong>Retention</strong><span>Archive contract, DPA, and records for 7 years</span></li></ul></article><article class="insight-panel"><table class="tprm-tier-table"><tbody><tr><td>Day 0</td><td><strong>Notify vendor</strong><small>Procurement communicates return/deletion requirements</small></td></tr><tr><td>30 days</td><td><strong>Export and deletion</strong><small>Receive data export and Certificate of Deletion</small></td></tr><tr><td>24 hours</td><td><strong>Revoke access</strong><small>Remove accounts, API keys, VPN, and repositories</small></td></tr><tr><td>6 months</td><td><strong>Post-termination audit</strong><small>Required for Tier 1 vendors</small></td></tr></tbody></table></article></div>
          <div class="excel-wrap"><table class="excel-table tprm-framework-table"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Offboarding task</th><th>Timeline</th><th>Owner</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Notify vendor of termination and data return/deletion requirements</td><td>Day 0</td><td>Procurement</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Receive complete data export in standard format</td><td>Within 30 days</td><td>IT</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Verify export completeness and integrity</td><td>Within 5 days of receipt</td><td>IT + Business Owner</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Revoke accounts, API keys, VPN, and repositories</td><td>Within 24 hours</td><td>IT Security</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Obtain Certificate of Deletion</td><td>Within 30 days</td><td>Procurement</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Verify deletion evidence</td><td>Within 5 days of certificate</td><td>IT Security</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Remove vendor from approved list and monitoring tools</td><td>Within 5 days</td><td>TPRM Team</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Post-termination audit for Tier 1</td><td>Within 6 months</td><td>Internal Audit</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Update RoPA for vendor removal</td><td>Within 30 days</td><td>Privacy Office</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Archive contract, DPA, and offboarding records</td><td>Per retention policy</td><td>Legal</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">GOVERNANCE & ORGANIZATION</p><h3>Roles and TPRM Committee</h3></div></div><div class="excel-wrap"><table class="excel-table tprm-framework-table"><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>CISO</td><td>Program owner, technical risk assessment, audit oversight</td></tr><tr><td>Privacy Officer</td><td>DPA compliance, RoPA entries, international transfers</td></tr><tr><td>Procurement</td><td>RFP, contract negotiation, financial due diligence</td></tr><tr><td>Legal</td><td>DPA/contract review, liability, regulatory interpretation</td></tr><tr><td>IT Security</td><td>Technical assessment, monitoring, access management</td></tr><tr><td>Business Owners</td><td>Vendor relationship, performance, renewal decisions</td></tr><tr><td>Internal Audit</td><td>Independent verification and annual effectiveness review</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="muted">TPRM Committee bertemu setiap kuartal dengan agenda onboarding Tier 1/2, high-risk review, escalated issues, process improvement, renewals, dan offboarding.</p>
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">AUDIT, ROADMAP & REFERENCES</p><h3>Implementation and standards</h3></div></div><div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Annual IT Audit</strong><span>Audit sample Tier 1, exercise contract clauses, verify RoPA/data flows, assess effectiveness</span></li><li><strong>Month 1-2</strong><span>Inventory vendors, obtain DPAs, tier risks, deploy questionnaire, train procurement</span></li><li><strong>Month 3-4</strong><span>Renegotiate high-risk contracts and deploy monitoring dashboards</span></li><li><strong>Month 5+</strong><span>Integrate annual audit cycle and launch TPRM Committee</span></li><li><strong>Ongoing</strong><span>Quarterly committee meetings and annual effectiveness review</span></li></ul></article><article class="insight-panel"><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>ISO 27001 Annex A.15</strong><span>Supplier relationships</span></li><li><strong>NIST SP 800-53 SA</strong><span>System and Services Acquisition</span></li><li><strong>NIST SP 800-161</strong><span>Supply Chain Risk Management</span></li><li><strong>GDPR Art. 28</strong><span>Processor obligations</span></li><li><strong>CCPA Section 1798.140</strong><span>Service Provider definition</span></li><li><strong>SOC 2 CC7.2, CC9.2</strong><span>Vendor management trust criteria</span></li></ul></article></div>
          <div class="tprm-grid"><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">TOOLS & TEMPLATES</p><h3>Supporting resources</h3></div></div><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>Vendor Tiering Matrix</strong><span>Detailed criteria</span></li><li><strong>Due Diligence Questionnaire</strong><span>Vendor assessment</span></li><li><strong>Standard DPA</strong><span>TPRM-specific contract</span></li><li><strong>Software Developer Checklist</strong><span>Technical verification</span></li><li><strong>General DPA Template</strong><span>Privacy contract</span></li><li><strong>RoPA Template</strong><span>Processing records</span></li></ul></article><article class="insight-panel"><div class="section-heading compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">COMMITTEE AGENDA</p><h3>Quarterly TPRM Committee</h3></div></div><ul class="tprm-list"><li><strong>1</strong><span>New Tier 1/2 vendor onboarding approvals</span></li><li><strong>2</strong><span>High-risk vendor performance and incidents</span></li><li><strong>3</strong><span>Escalated issues and remediation status</span></li><li><strong>4</strong><span>Policy and process improvement proposals</span></li><li><strong>5</strong><span>Upcoming renewals and offboarding</span></li></ul></article></div>
        </section>
</template>
